# Messora edge proxy. EDGE_MODE picks how TLS is done (docs/INSTALL.md):
#
#   proxy (default)  Plain HTTP on :80 for every host. TLS ends in front of
#                    Caddy (Traefik / Dokploy, a load balancer) or nowhere
#                    (local use, E2E). SITE_ADDRESS may still name one
#                    domain for automatic HTTPS on a single-domain server.
#   caddy            Caddy is the internet edge: one wildcard certificate
#                    for TENANT_BASE_DOMAIN and *.TENANT_BASE_DOMAIN by
#                    DNS-01 (name.com), on-demand certificates for the
#                    companies' verified custom domains.
#
# The routes are the same in both modes (routes.caddy).
import modes/{$EDGE_MODE:proxy}.caddy
